# Issue tracking (GitHub + Cursor)

**Single backlog:** [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/Joeydekruis/dockyrd/issues) on this repo. No Linear, no dual-tracking.

| Who | System | Owns |
|-|--|--|
| **Maintainers / community** | **GitHub** | Labels, milestones, triage, closing verified work |
| **Agents / contributors** | **Cursor + git** | Implementation, specs in repo, PRs or pushes to `development` |

Process guide: [`docs/project/github-workflow.md`](../../docs/project/github-workflow.md).

---

## Work tracks (pick one)

| Track | When | What to do |
|-|--|--|
| **Feature** | New feature or **big** product/architecture adjustment | **GitHub issue** + harness (discuss → plan → [design if UI] → generate → review). Local `docs/project/issues/<n>/` holds AC (`n` = issue number). |
| **Direct** | Feedback, polish, bugfixes in chat | **No** planner, **no** GitHub issue required. Implement on `development`. Light notes only. |

When a **new feature** is raised in Cursor: **create or update a GitHub issue** (via `gh issue create` / web) before or while planning.

---

## Separation of concerns

| Artefact | Owns |
|--|--|
| **GitHub issue `#n`** | Title, labels, milestone, discussion, close when verified |
| **`docs/project/issues/<n>/spec.md`** | Feature AC (planner) |
| **`docs/project/issues/<n>/rubric.md`** | Done-criteria; reviewers |
| **`docs/project/feedback/<n>/`** | Generator/reviewer iterations |
| **`docs/project/project.md`** | Product truth, lifecycle |
| **`docs/project/roadmap.md`** | M0–M5 phases (update when features land) |
| **`docs/project/sprints.md`** | Sprint ↔ milestone mapping |
| **`development` branch** | Day-to-day commits; push when shipping issue work |
| **`docs/project/generator-state.md`** | Agent session handoff — not the backlog |

---

## Issue ID convention

- **Features:** folder key = GitHub issue number: `docs/project/issues/12/`, `docs/project/feedback/12/`.
- **Direct:** optional `#n` if someone filed a bug; do not invent duplicate issues.
- Spec frontmatter includes `github: https://github.com/Joeydekruis/dockyrd/issues/n`.

---

## Feature track MUST

1. **Exist on GitHub** (create if missing when the feature is discussed).
2. **Stay aligned** — issue body links to local spec after planning.
3. **Harness** — plan → generate → review (lighten for micro-S/S).
4. **Handoff** — commit + push → evidence comment on issue per [github-handoff](github-handoff.mdc). Do not close the issue.

## Sprint pickup (HARD)

When the human says **“pick up sprint X”**:

1. Resolve sprint X via GitHub **milestone** (see `sprints.md`).
2. Pick up **all** open issues in that milestone.
3. Each: implement → test → commit + push → GitHub handoff comment.

---

## Direct track MUST NOT

- Require GitHub issues for tiny fixes.
- Spin full harness unless the change is actually a **big** adjustment (then Feature track).

---

## Git / delivery

- Work on **`development`** only (see [git-branch](git-branch.mdc)).
- Feature finish: tests → `CHANGELOG.md` patch bump → commit + push (`Fixes #n` or `Refs #n`) → issue comment.
- **`main`:** merge only when Joey asks — skill **push-to-main**.

---

## What we do NOT do

- Linear or any second issue tracker.
- Per-feature git branches (`feature/*`).
- Close Feature issues without maintainer verification after handoff.
